# Force LF for fixed-format Fortran and shell/build tooling regardless
# of the checking-out machine's core.autocrlf setting -- the F77
# 72-column lint rule is column-sensitive, and a CRLF checkout adds a
# 73rd byte per line that the rule (correctly) rejects. All source
# files are already stored as LF; this just keeps checkouts that way
# (some CI runner images default to autocrlf-style conversion).
*.F      text eol=lf
*.f      text eol=lf
*.F90    text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
